# The characterization harness's stubs are source, not generated binaries.
#
# They live in a directory called bin/ because that is what goes on PATH, and the rule above swallowed
# them: `git add hack/test` staged the driver and every golden file and silently left out the two files
# that make the harness a harness. A fresh checkout would then prepend a directory containing nothing to
# PATH and run the REAL aws and the REAL sleep against a real account.
!/hack/test/spot-lifecycle/bin/
!/hack/test/spot-lifecycle/bin/*

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Go test artifacts
*.out
*.test

# Claude Code personal overrides
.claude/settings.local.json

# M6 kind E2E run artifact (curated evidence lives in hack/m6-kind-e2e.md)

# stray local build of cmd/benchharness, anchored so it cannot also swallow new files under cmd/benchharness/
/benchharness

# stray local build of cmd/queuelabrun, anchored so it cannot also swallow new files under cmd/queuelabrun/
/queuelabrun

# Raw chaos-run records were excluded here, and queuelab inherited the rule without anyone asking whether it
# fit. It does not. This lab's thesis is that the record outlives the terminal and that a conclusion nobody
# can re-derive is prose -- and its records sat outside version control while committed documents told
# readers to run `queuelabrun -compare 'ex/e14-*.json'` against files that do not ship.
#
# It cost what you would expect. A pre-registration fixed the GPU session's baseline at a figure assembled at
# a shell from records that were then deleted, and the number appears in no record that exists. Git is the
# notary a pre-registration needs; declining it left half the evidence with an mtime and nothing else.
#
# So run records are committed and the rest of ex/ -- scratch output, ad-hoc blobs -- is not. The whole
# directory is 248 KB.
ex/*
!ex/*.json

# Paid-session output, which belongs beside the session rather than in the source tree.
#
# hack/m5b-arms.sh writes a run directory per invocation -- traces, manifests, raw JSONL, the report -- and
# hack/m5b-gpu-session.sh writes .m5b-rate for the second shell to read. Three runs of these landed in the
# repository because a commit used `git add -A`, which is how ~40 files of experiment output ended up in a
# source history that has to stay readable.
#
# The evidence still matters and is kept: it is copied out of the working tree when a run finishes. What
# does not belong here is a growing pile of one-off measurements that no code reads.
hack/m5b-run-*/
hack/m5c-run-*/
# The M5-c SESSION's own directory, which is not the matrix's.
#
# hack/m5c-matrix.sh writes hack/m5c-run-<stamp> and is covered by the line above. hack/m5c-gpu-session.sh
# writes hack/m5c-<stamp>, one level out, and holds about 100 MB: the source archive plus the gateway and
# harness binaries it ships to the instance. The pattern above does not match it, so the first failed run
# left all of that untracked in the tree -- one `git add -A` from the mistake this block was written about.
hack/m5c-2*/
# The capacity ladder's session directory, which is the same script under a different OUT.
#
# hack/m5c-gpu-session.sh writes wherever OUT points, and the ladder runs use hack/ladder-<stamp> so that a
# ladder's evidence is not filed among the sharing matrix's. Ignored for the reason above and for the one
# below: this runner REFUSES TO START when the tree is dirty, so a run's own output directory makes the
# next run impossible. That is exactly what happened -- a killed ladder session left hack/ladder-<stamp>
# untracked and the relaunch refused, with the card already released.
hack/ladder-*/
# Microtest output: instance ids, user-data, and the raw results, which are copied into
# docs/evidence when a run produces something worth keeping.
hack/microtest-*/
# The device-observation session writes a run directory per invocation. Ignored for the same reason as the
# others, and for one more: this runner refuses to start when the tree is dirty, so its own output would
# otherwise stop the next run.
hack/qlgpu-*/
hack/pop-*/
hack/m5b-gpu-session-evidence.log
.m5b-rate

# Captures written by hack/capture-evidence.sh, and tracked on purpose.
#
# The run directories these come from are ignored and do not survive, so a number nobody can read later was
# not worth measuring. Placed LAST because git applies the final matching rule: earlier in this file `docs/*`
# hides the directory and `*.md` hides the index, and a negation above either of them does nothing.
!docs/captures/
!docs/captures/**
